This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
\begin{split}
\begin{aligned}
\left\{\begin{aligned}
&\Delta^2u-\Delta u=u\left(\lambda+\int_{\mathbb{R}^3}\frac{\Omega(y,u)\Omega(z,u)}{|x-y|}dx\right),\quad x\in\mathbb{R}^3,\\
&\int_{\mathbb{ \mathbb{R}^3}}\left(|\Delta u|^2+u^2\right)dx=3\lambda^2,
\end{aligned}\right.
\end{aligned}\end{align*} under appropriate assumptions on the function $\Omega$. By establishing a fibering structure and applying variational methods, we successfully prove the existence of normalized ground state solutions for this problem.
